   "desc": "AWS Chicago User Group RSVP with IndyPy to get the Zoom info: [https://sixfeetup.zoom.us/meeting/register/QiJIN4D8QMeULjCmI7Rftw#/registration ](https://sixfeetup.zoom.us/meeting/register/QiJIN4D8QMeULjCmI7Rftw#/registration) **About** Django just turned 21, and Python web development keeps evolving. What's changing in Django's open-source community? And how do you decide between Django and FastAPI for your next project? Join us for two talks exploring the future of Django and the real-world tradeoffs between two popular Python frameworks. Discover what's new, learn from production experience, and walk away with practical insights for your next project. Join us either in person or remotely for our hybrid event! * **IN PERSON:** E-gineering in Indianapolis, IN * **REMOTE:** [Register to get the Zoom link.](https://sixfeetup.zoom.us/meeting/register/QiJIN4D8QMeULjCmI7Rftw) **AGENDA** **7:10 - 7:25pm: Meet Your Tribe (Icebreakers)** Meet fellow Python enthusiasts, make new connections, and kick off the evening with fun icebreakers. **7:25 - 7:30pm:** Announcements **7:30 - 7:55pm: “What's New in Contributing to Django?” by Tim Schilling, Better Simple Django & Python Consultant** Django just turned 21, but there's more to celebrate than its longevity. Over the past three years, its community has introduced mentorship opportunities, dedicated sprint events, and a formal process for shipping new features. Tim will explore how these initiatives are making Django more sustainable, welcoming, and easier to contribute to, and why its community is one of the framework's greatest strengths. **7:55 - 8:20pm: “Batteries-Included vs. Speed: The Django/FastAPI Debate” by Calvin Hendryx-Parker, Six Feet Up CTO and AWS Hero** Django or FastAPI? The answer depends on what you're building. Drawing on years of production experience with both frameworks, Calvin will compare Django's batteries-included approach with FastAPI's lightweight, API-first design. Learn where each framework shines, how they differ, and what matters most when choosing the right tool for your product, team, and long-term maintenance needs. No winner, just practical guidance for making a smarter decision. **8:20 - 8:30pm:** Door Prizes **8:30 - 9pm: Networking & General Discussion**",
